author: claude
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Contamination is defined as forward reachability from the candidate's training data to the evaluation set over an enumerated set of provenance edge types; overlap is decided on content-addressed identity and never on labels; promotion exits non-zero and prints the connecting path as an ordered list of artifact identities and edge types; the printed path is stable across runs for the same graph; the check runs before any score is computed or written so a contaminated score never reaches history; an uncontaminated candidate promotes; there is no flag that downgrades the refusal to a warning
resolution: Added test/lineage.test.ts exercising contamination traversal and the promotion refusal; refusal verified revert-proof.
expected_result: Promotion refuses when the eval set is forward-reachable from training data over provenance edges; prints a stable path; uncontaminated candidate promotes.
actual_result: test/lineage.test.ts passes; index.ts and lineage.ts at 100/100/100 lines/branches/functions.
